This task implements all of PRD-A in a single coordinated commit series. The implementation breaks down into six sub-areas:

**1. build.rs files (rust/limux-cli/, rust/limux-host-linux/, rust/limux-control/)**
Each build.rs must:
- Run `git rev-parse --short=12 HEAD` for SHA (fallback: literal `unknown`, never fabricated)
- Run `git status --porcelain` for dirty flag (non-empty = dirty; fallback: `unknown`)
- Emit `cargo:rustc-env=LIMUX_BUILD_SHA=<sha>`, `LIMUX_BUILD_DIRTY=<true|false|unknown>`, `LIMUX_BUILD_PROFILE=<debug|release>`
- Emit `cargo:rerun-if-changed` for: `.git` (may be a file redirecting to `.git/worktrees/<name>/HEAD`), worktree index path, workspace `Cargo.toml`, `Cargo.lock`, and all workspace path-dependency source trees (`rust/*/Cargo.toml`, crate `build.rs` files, crate `src/` trees)
- If dirty-flag rerun cannot be made reliable across all workspace source/index changes, report dirty as `unknown` instead of stale `false`

```rust
// Pseudo-code for build.rs
use std::process::Command;

fn main() {
    let sha = Command::new("git")
        .args(["rev-parse", "--short=12", "HEAD"])
        .output()
        .ok()
        .filter(|o| o.status.success())
        .and_then(|o| String::from_utf8(o.stdout).ok())
        .map(|s| s.trim().to_string())
        .unwrap_or_else(|| "unknown".to_string());

    let dirty = if sha == "unknown" {
        "unknown".to_string()
    } else {
        // Check if we can reliably track all dirty inputs
        let porcelain = Command::new("git")
            .args(["status", "--porcelain"])
            .output()
            .ok()
            .filter(|o| o.status.success())
            .map(|o| String::from_utf8(o.stdout).unwrap_or_default())
            .unwrap_or_default();
        if porcelain.trim().is_empty() { "false" } else { "true" }.to_string()
    };

    let profile = if cfg!(debug_assertions) { "debug" } else { "release" };

    println!("cargo:rustc-env=LIMUX_BUILD_SHA={}", sha);
    println!("cargo:rustc-env=LIMUX_BUILD_DIRTY={}", dirty);
    println!("cargo:rustc-env=LIMUX_BUILD_PROFILE={}", profile);

    // Emit rerun-if-changed for git HEAD, index, and workspace sources
    // Handle .git-as-file worktree redirect
    println!("cargo:rerun-if-changed=.git");
    println!("cargo:rerun-if-changed=Cargo.toml");
    println!("cargo:rerun-if-changed=Cargo.lock");
    // Walk rust/*/Cargo.toml, rust/*/build.rs, rust/*/src/**/*.rs
    // ...
}
```

**2. BuildInfo injection in limux-core**
- Add a `BuildInfo` struct to `limux-core`:
```rust
