## Part 3: pane.action Bridge Route (US-2)

### ControlCommand Variant (lib.rs)
```rust
// rust/limux-core/src/lib.rs
pub enum ControlCommand {
    // ... existing variants ...
    PaneAction {
        pane_ref: String,
        action: PaneAction,
    },
}

pub enum PaneAction {
    SetFlagColor { color: String },
    ClearFlagColor,
}

pub const ALLOWED_FLAG_COLORS: &[&str] = &[
    "red", "orange", "yellow", "green", "blue", "purple",
];

// Validation: allowlist match BEFORE any string reaches CSS
pub fn validate_flag_color(color: &str) -> Result<(), String> {
    if ALLOWED_FLAG_COLORS.contains(&color) {
        Ok(())
    } else {
        Err(format!("Invalid flag color '{}'. Allowed: {:?}", color, ALLOWED_FLAG_COLORS))
    }
}
```

### Bridge Route
Add `pane.action` to both the standalone dispatcher (limux-core) and the live GTK bridge path so both accept the new actions.

```rust
// window.rs — handle pane action
fn handle_pane_action(&mut self, pane_ref: &str, action: &PaneAction) {
    let pane_id = self.resolve_pane_ref(pane_ref);
    match action {
        PaneAction::SetFlagColor { color } => {
            validate_flag_color(color)?;  // allowlist before CSS
            if let Some(pane) = self.panes.get_mut(&pane_id) {
                pane.set_flag_color(Some(color.to_string()));
                self.apply_flag_color_visuals(&pane_id, color);
                self.mark_session_dirty();
            }
        }
        PaneAction::ClearFlagColor => {
            if let Some(pane) = self.panes.get_mut(&pane_id) {
                pane.set_flag_color(None);
                self.clear_flag_color_visuals(&pane_id);
                self.mark_session_dirty();
            }
        }
    }
}

// Apply visuals: CSS class on pane chrome + edge accent
fn apply_flag_color_visuals(&self, pane_id: &str, color: &str) {
    if let Some(pane) = self.panes.get(pane_id) {
        let css_class = format!("limux-pane-flag-{}", color);
        pane.chrome_widget.add_css_class(&css_class);
        pane.content_overlay.add_css_class(&css_class);
    }
}
```

