4. **Avoid clobbering retained files**: Use timestamp-based or sequence-based naming for retained files. Before moving active to retained, check for name collisions and skip or rename if collision exists. Move-aside semantics comply with no-delete policy.
```rust
fn rotate_active_to_retained(active: &Path, retained_dir: &Path, retention: &Retention) -> Result<(), LogError> {
    if !active.exists() { return Ok(()) }
    let timestamp = SystemTime::now().duration_since(UNIX_EPOCH)?.as_nanos();
    let mut retained_path = retained_dir.join(format!("limux.{}.log", timestamp));
    // Collision check
    let mut counter = 0;
    while retained_path.exists() {
        counter += 1;
        retained_path = retained_dir.join(format!("limux.{}.{}.log", timestamp, counter));
    }
    fs::rename(active, &retained_path)?; // move-aside, not delete
    // Enforce retention count (remove oldest retained beyond count — but only retained files, never incident log)
    enforce_retention_count(retained_dir, retention.max_retained_count)?;
    Ok(())
}
```

