```rust
fn dequeue_and_launch(&mut self) -> Result<(), ResumeError> {
    if self.paused || self.active_count >= self.max_concurrency { return Ok(()) }
    if let Some(req) = self.items.pop_front() {
        if !verify_exact_surface_identity(&req.target_surface_id) {
            return Err(ResumeError::SurfaceMismatch);
        }
        self.active_count += 1;
        launch_agent(&req.launch_metadata)?;
    }
    Ok(())
}
```

4. **Multi-signal pressure sampling**:
   - Sample bounded signals at a controlled interval (not busy-loop):
     - `MemAvailable` from `/proc/meminfo`
     - Swap activity from `/proc/swaps` or `/proc/vmstat`
     - Process RSS growth (own process)
     - Active launch count (from queue)
     - WSL I/O evidence (e.g., `/proc/diskstats` inflight, D-state census)
   - PSI may inform but may not independently block or release work.
```rust
struct PressureMonitor {
    mem_available: u64, // bytes
    swap_delta: i64, // bytes since last sample
    rss_growth: i64, // bytes since last sample
    active_launches: usize,
    wsl_io_inflight: u32,
    pause_threshold: PressureThreshold,
    resume_threshold: PressureThreshold, // hysteresis: resume threshold less strict than pause
}

fn check_pressure(&self) -> PressureState {
    if self.mem_available < self.pause_threshold.mem_min
        || self.swap_delta > self.pause_threshold.swap_delta_max
        || self.rss_growth > self.pause_threshold.rss_growth_max {
        return PressureState::Pause;
    }
    if self.mem_available > self.resume_threshold.mem_min
        && self.swap_delta <= self.resume_threshold.swap_delta_max
        && self.rss_growth <= self.resume_threshold.rss_growth_max {
        return PressureState::Resume;
    }
    PressureState::Hold // hysteresis band
}
```

5. **Hysteresis behavior**:
   - Pause admission on pressure → stop dequeuing new agents.
   - Resume only after hysteresis (pressure drops below resume threshold, not just below pause threshold).
   - Never terminate already-running agents as part of admission control.

6. **Cancellation**:
   - Cancel queued (not-yet-launched) agents without affecting running sessions.
   - Mark cancelled agents with `Cancelled` status and `UserChoice` suspension reason.
```rust
fn cancel_queued(&mut self, agent_id: &AgentId) -> Result<(), ResumeError> {
    if let Some(req) = self.items.iter_mut().find(|r| &r.agent_id == agent_id) {
        if req.status == ResumeStatus::Queued {
            req.status = ResumeStatus::Cancelled;
            return Ok(())
        }
        return Err(ResumeError::AlreadyLaunching)
    }
    Err(ResumeError::NotFound)
}
```

